==========================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- the amplification law, derived and then verified numerically before any data is touched
==========================================================================================================================
  nu = 1/(1-e^-u), u = sqrt(y)  =>  d ln nu/du = -1/(e^u - 1),  d ln y = 2 du/u
                                =>  m(y) = d ln nu/d ln y = -u/(2(e^u - 1))
  A coherent shift ln g_bar -> ln g_bar + d moves ln g_obs by (1+m) d at fixed a_0;
  a shift ln a_0 -> ln a_0 + A moves it by -m A.  Compensation gives A = (1+m) d / m.

        y = g_bar/a0        m(y)      LAMBDA(y) = d ln a0 / d ln Upsilon
