    SPARC last point (z~0)              147      127    0.86           8.920e-11        -0.021
    RC100 (z 0.6-2.5)                   100        0    0.00                  --            --
    MSA-3D golden (z 0.6-1.7)            23        0    0.00                  --            --
    KROSS stars-only (z~0.9)            381       10    0.03           8.343e-11        -0.050
    MUSE-DARK II lensed (z 0.5-1.45)       95       29    0.31           8.274e-11        -0.054
  [PASS] k02-4 THE GATE SPLITS THE HIGH-REDSHIFT ARCHIVE IN TWO, and that is the finding: not one of the 123 galaxies in the two resolved-kinematics surveys is observed at an acceleration where a_0 can be read with a lever near -1, while the LENSED dwarf sample passes in bulk.  The redshift axis is not systematics-limited by accident; the massive-disc surveys are observed in the wrong regime, and lensed low-mass galaxies are the class that is not   (RC100 0/100 and MSA-3D 0/23 pass y <= 0.186, against MUSE-DARK II 29/95 and SPARC's last points 127/147)

